From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: guard hwmon read on PHY reset and suspend

When an RTL822x/RTL826x PHY is suspended or undergoing its soft-reset
sequence (e.g. RTL826x MMD30.0x145 in rtl826x_config_init()), MDIO reads
from TSRR/TSSR can return stale data or a floating 0xffff bus value that
decodes to a bogus -0.5 C temperature.

Return -ENODATA immediately when phydev->suspended is set (checked
directly as phydev->suspended is a 1-bit bitfield in struct phy_device),
and return -EIO if phy_read_mmd() returns 0xffff on TSRR or TSSR.

Origin: local, xr1710g #415
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_hwmon.c
@@ -28,18 +28,25 @@ static int rtl822x_hwmon_read(struct dev
 	struct phy_device *phydev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int raw;
 
+	if (phydev->suspended)
+		return -ENODATA;
+
 	switch (attr) {
 	case hwmon_temp_input:
 		raw = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, RTL822X_VND2_TSRR);
 		if (raw < 0)
 			return raw;
+		if (raw == 0xffff)
+			return -EIO;
 		*val = rtl822x_hwmon_get_temp(raw & 0x3ff);
 		break;
 	case hwmon_temp_max:
 		/* Chip reduces speed to 1G if threshold is exceeded */
 		raw = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2, RTL822X_VND2_TSSR);
 		if (raw < 0)
 			return raw;
+		if (raw == 0xffff)
+			return -EIO;
 		*val = rtl822x_hwmon_get_temp(raw >> 6);
 		break;
 	default:
